=== Task 2.6 NOT COMPLETED for DeepStream, Savant and native processes (no code change; needs a spec/design decision)
# Findings at commit 5246d2a1 (source references, no runtime execution):
# - DeepStream/Savant SDK workers and vast_checkpoint_source / vast_native_gst_probe are children of
#   scripts/checkpoint_runtime.py run_worker_processes (Popen stderr=PIPE, :1459-1466 and :1529-1536).
#   capture_stderr (:1338-1361) keeps only a 16 KiB in-memory tail per process; it reaches evidence only
#   inside a failure ContractError (final_stderr_tails, :1991-2001). On success the tail is discarded, so the
#   native line "[native-probe|checkpoint-source][wall-clock] max_clamp_ns=" is not retained.
# - No Python code parses that line.
# - The in-container owners write their summaries under native_runtime/ (deepstream_runtime_manifest.json,
#   native_stdio_audit, reset/cohort audits), which retire_owned_runtime_output_v1 removes at the end of the arm;
#   the SDK worker exit summary (run_fd_worker) is not persisted because fd 1 is reserved for the nvstreammux audit.
# - Everything that survives (terminal status, publication acceptance, CSV evidence, engine process capture
#   terminal: stdout/stderr only as size+sha256) is validated with exact field sets downstream
#   (e.g. checkpoint_deepstream_publication_runtime_v3.py:944-984).
# Therefore "existing persisted evidence of the process" does not exist on the success path for these
# processes, and adding max_clamp_ns there means a new persisted field or file through strict validators.
